      "latin": "comprimō, comprimere, compressī, compressum",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "squeeze or press together, compress",
      "comment": "Our practical choice for squishing something soft or squashing it down; the object supplies the soft/wet quality. English “squeeze,” “squish,” “squash” and “crush” overlap. These Latin choices distinguish compression, extraction, pounding and grinding; they are not four rigid one-to-one equivalents."
    }
